# The corpus revision: the `tenferro-einsum-benchmark` checkout whose
# `data/instances/*.json` the harness loads. It is an external input, not a
# dependency of the measured library, so `scripts/setup_extern_deps.sh`
# materialises it as `extern/tenferro-einsum-benchmark` and nothing is vendored:
# the instance files stay the source of truth for shapes, equations and the two
# declared contraction orders.
#
# There is no release to pin to, so this names the corpus's `main` at the revision
# the campaign was built against: 14 instances, one JSON file per problem, each
# carrying `name`, `format_string`, `shapes`, `dtype` and `paths.{opt_size,opt_flops}`.
# A corpus change is a different corpus, and the page records this revision in its
# own section so a number is never read against the wrong instance set.
